# Files whose job is to name identifiers that do not resolve.
#
# The citation gate asks that every identifier a change writes into a file exists
# on the spec's default branch. Most of the time that is exactly right: a number
# in a refusal message or a doc heading is a citation to whoever follows it, and
# a slipped digit sends them nowhere.
#
# These four are the other case. A renderer that proves it strikes a withdrawn
# requirement through has to render one; a reader that proves it refuses a number
# past the ceiling has to ask for one past the ceiling. Written out of real
# requirement numbers instead, they would pass today and start failing the week
# the spec moves — which is the gate making the tests worse rather than better.
#
# Exact paths, never a pattern, and a path that is not here any more is refused
# rather than skipped: the day one of these moves, the gate says which line to
# correct. Every one of them is printed on every run, because an exemption nobody
# sees is an exemption nobody revisits.
